EXP-0053 postmortem.

The mirror experiment is complete: primary and mirror White match in both healthy and abnormal batches. The abnormal four-frame target ring alternates between approximately +2.72 and -8.0, with thousands of zero samples and an all-black mid texture. Do not move the smoother or remove smoothing.

The input identity failure is now specific. onSwapChainResize clears gInputFinalColorNative. SetTextureHook can repopulate it only while gInTaauDraw is true, and that thread-local window exists only around gOriginalDraw. The replacement branch suppresses gOriginalDraw, so after resize there is no semantic recapture path and pickInputs falls back to an unwritten/alternating RTV candidate.

A single forwarded frame is not a sufficient contract: an existing disarm/rearm interval may precede RTV/material readiness. Use a bounded budget of four forwarded draws, stop immediately after a render-size fmt26 match, reset the material log throttle on resize, and warn on budget exhaustion. Do not retain stale native pointers, parse the declarator attachment, or select another frozen candidate; docs/specs/vv.md sections 22-31 already refute those alternatives.

Success requires both mechanism and resulting continuity: semantic nonzero with current render dimensions and match=1, then a stable target ring and non-saturated final. If semantic remains null, the experiment fails without interpreting exposure behavior further.
